/**
Multi-Set

Header File:
<set>

--> Same as set
--> Allows duplicates
--> No random access

(i)Declaration: multiset<int> s
(ii)Insertion: s.insert (val)
(iii)Deletion : s.erase (val) or s.erase (pos)

        To remove only one occurance of element
        --> Using iterator find 1 st occurance 
        --> delete
    eg:
    it = ms.find(10)
    if(it!=ms.end())
        ms.erase(it)
(iv)equal_range (ele) : returns two iterator
        --> first occurance of element 
        --> second : after last occurance of element

    eg : it = ms.equal_range(3)
        for (auto i = ms.first(); i!=ms.second();i++)
        cout<<*i;

(v) Index : distance(s.begin(),i)
